large and small dairy farms? Econometric evidence from three wisconsin communities</article-title><source>Agric Resour Econ Rev</source><volume>31</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>28</fpage><lpage>38</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ehp0115-000317"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>Gacke v. Pork XTRA, L.L.C</collab> June 2004. Case No. 147 /02-0417, Iowa Supreme Court, Des Moines, IA.</citation></ref><ref id="b22-ehp0115-000317"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Goldschmidt</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group>. 1978. Agribusiness and the rural community. In: As You Sow: Three Studies in the Social Consequence of Agribusiness. Montclair, NJ:Allenheld, Osmun, and Co. [First published as Small Business and the Community: A study in Central Valley of California on effects of scale of farm operations. Report of the Special Committee to Study Problems of American Small Business, United States Senate, December 23, 1946, U.S. Government Printing Office, Washington, DC, 1946.]</citation></ref><ref id="b23-ehp0115-000317"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Gomez</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group>. 2000. Impacts of concentration in hog production on economic growth in rural Illinois: an economic analysis. American Agricultural Economics Association Annual Meeting, 31 July-2 August 2000, Tampa, FL. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://agecon.lib.umn.edu/cgi-bin/view.pl">http://agecon.lib.umn.edu/cgi-bin/view.pl</ext-link> [accessed 5 January 2007].</citation></ref><ref id="b24-ehp0115-000317"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Hamed</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name></person-group>. 1999. The Impacts of Animal Feedi